# Shell scripts and SQL run inside Linux containers. A checkout with
# core.autocrlf on turns "#!/bin/sh" into "#!/bin/sh\r", and an image built
# from it exits at once with "no such file or directory" for the entrypoint;
# psql tolerates a stray \r in a migration, the shell does not. Pin both to LF
# on every checkout, whatever the client's autocrlf setting. setup.sh already
# strips \r from .env for the same reason.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
